# Variety prediction with logistic regression (RGB, snv)

Leaf mean at three bands (R 640.0 nm, G 548.5 nm, B 461.0 nm) -> SNV -> standardise -> multinomial logistic regression, C chosen inside each training split. Same 5 row folds as the 204-band run; every leaf predicted by the model that never saw its row.

**Balanced accuracy: 0.500** (95% CI 0.471-0.530; chance 0.25). Macro-F1: 0.497.

Confusion matrix (rows = true variety, columns = predicted):

| true \ predicted | Baco | Cab Franc | Chardonnay | Vidal | total |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| **Baco** | 99 | 4 | 70 | 75 | 248 |
| **Cab Franc** | 37 | 97 | 23 | 93 | 250 |
| **Chardonnay** | 49 | 1 | 186 | 14 | 250 |
| **Vidal** | 69 | 45 | 19 | 117 | 250 |

| variety | precision | recall | F1 | n | ROC AUC (one vs rest) |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Baco | 0.390 | 0.399 | 0.394 | 248 | 0.612 |
| Cab Franc | 0.660 | 0.388 | 0.489 | 250 | 0.776 |
| Chardonnay | 0.624 | 0.744 | 0.679 | 250 | 0.871 |
| Vidal | 0.391 | 0.468 | 0.426 | 250 | 0.720 |

## Per fold (held-out row)

| test row | chosen C | test leaves | balanced accuracy |
|---|---|---|---|
| R1 | 1 | 200 | 0.455 |
| R2 | 0.1 | 200 | 0.485 |
| R3 | 0.1 | 198 | 0.584 |
| R4 | 0.1 | 200 | 0.540 |
| R5 | 1000 | 200 | 0.435 |

Caveat: 'variety' also carries anything acquired together with it (imaging day, lighting, leaf handling), so a high score shows the spectra separate the varieties, not that cultivar biology alone is the cause.

